      "body": "\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\nTerratorch models (Prithvi, TerraMind, etc.) were already supported in vLLM via the\r\nexisting `Terratorch` model class. This PR extends that support to the **V2 engine**\r\nby fixing three issues that prevent Terratorch pooling models from loading or running\r\nunder the V2 model runner.\r\n\r\n- **`terratorch.py`** — `SupportsMultiModal.get_language_model()` walks child modules\r\n  looking for a `VllmModel` instance. `Terratorch` is a pure pooling model with no\r\n  inner language model, so the default implementation always raises\r\n  `NotImplementedError`. Adding `get_language_model(self): return self` satisfies the\r\n  interface contract and removes the need for a workaround subclass in the terratorch\r\n  package.\r\n\r\n- **`pooling_runner.py`** — The V2 pooling runner validates the selected task against\r\n  an explicit allowlist. Terratorch models register task type `\"plugin\"` to signal that\r\n  output post-processing is fully owned by the model plugin. This type was absent from\r\n  the allowlist, causing the V2 engine to reject the model at startup.\r\n\r\n- **`rejection_sampler.py`** — `get_max_chunk_logits` divides by `vocab_size`. During\r\n  V2 warm-up this is called for all models including pooling models. Terratorch has no\r\n  text vocabulary (`vocab_size == 0`), triggering a `ZeroDivisionError` even though\r\n  speculative decoding is never used for pooling models. An early-return guard when\r\n  `vocab_size == 0` prevents the crash.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\nRun Terratorch inference (Prithvi / TerraMind) with `VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER=1` and\r\nverify the model loads, warms up, and produces correct embeddings end-to-end.\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\nTerratorch models load and run correctly under the V2 engine. All three failure modes\r\n(startup rejection, `NotImplementedError`, `ZeroDivisionError`) are resolved.\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\r\n- [ ] The test plan, such as providing test command.\r\n- [ ] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\r\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
